        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63111,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63112,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> gliomatosis peritonei</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63113,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63114,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneum, omentum, lymph nodes {24421855}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63115,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually have symptoms related to an ovarian teratoma. However, gliomatosis can cause abdominal/pelvic pain due to the formation of masses, or abnormalities may be seen on imaging studies when gliomatosis occurs as recurrent disease after ovarian immature teratomas have been treated and the patient has normal serum markers. In these circumstances, gliomatosis becomes part of the so-called growing teratoma syndrome {26564007}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63116,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gliomatosis is rare. It occurs over a wide age range but is more common in young patients. It can be associated with immature teratomas, mature cystic teratomas, mixed germ cell tumours, and ventriculoperitoneal shunts {26564007}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63117,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Proposed theories include maturation of implanted ovarian teratomatous elements and metaplasia of pluripotent M&uuml;llerian stem cells or supraperitoneal mesenchymal cells {15188134; 11438453}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63118,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63119,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It typically occurs as miliary lesions, measuring a few millimetres in size; however, larger lesions can be encountered.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63120,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are discrete nodules of mature glial tissue that are occasionally associated with inflammation, haemorrhage, and fibrosis. Infrequently, gliomatosis is associated with endometriosis {24421855}. Immunohistochemistry shows the nodules to be positive for GFAP and SOX2 and variably positive for S100 {26564007}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63121,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63122,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63123,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> mature glial cell aggregates; absence of other teratomatous elements.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63124,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>See comment on the staging of gliomatosis peritonei in <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/91\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Immature teratoma of the ovary</em>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T08:05:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63125,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Gliomatosis has a favourable outcome {25594144; 26033179}. However, morbidity related to the expansive and compressive nature of enlarged glial masses {28656118} and rare malignant transformation, usually to high-grade gliomas, have been documented {2048608; 9195578}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T17:14:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]